  <name>SonicTune</name>
  <summary>Native Linux YouTube Music client</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      SonicTune is a FOSS YouTube Music client for Linux, built for performance,
      privacy, and power users. It runs as a background daemon — so playback
      continues even if the UI crashes — with a QML frontend that talks to it
      over D-Bus.
    </p>
    <p>Features include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>256 kbps AAC playback via libmpv (hardware-decoded, gapless)</li>
      <li>OAuth login (TV device code flow) + cookie import fallback</li>
      <li>Search and browse YouTube Music (Home, Charts, Library)</li>
      <li>Synced lyrics via LRCLIB</li>
      <li>MPRIS integration (KDE/GNOME media controls)</li>
      <li>Album art pipeline with on-disk LRU cache</li>
      <li>Queue management with shuffle, repeat, drag-to-reorder</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
